accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report  ms 09  removed_accession_id  case  ms 09  removed_accession_id  removed_patient_name  date taken  removed_date source care unit  same day surgery  wacc 3 path subspecialty service  breast 1 results to  michele annette gadd  m d  resident  evan farkash  m d   ph d  signed out by  ronald balassanian  m d  clinical data  the patient is a 43 year old woman with a prior diagnosis of biphasic fibroepithelial tumor by core biopsy  final diagnosis  a  breast  left   excision  1  fibroadenoma with cellular stroma  2  atypical ductal hyperplasia  focal  3  fibrocystic changes  4  healing biopsy site  see note  note  the main specimen  part a  was received fragmented  limiting assessment of the growth pattern  sections reveal a fibroepithelial lesion with a mixed intracanalicular and pericanalicular growth pattern  notably  a frond like growth pattern and a pushing or infiltrative margin to suggest a diagnosis of phyllodes tumor are not appreciated in this sample  the stroma exhibits a mixture of hyalinized areas as well as geographic zones of myxoid change  in some areas  there is increased stromal cellularity  and the nuclei of the stromal cells appear enlarged with irregular contours and prominent nucleoli  only rare mitotic figures are identified  these findings may be interpreted as atypical in some settings  however  in the absence of other morphologic features of a phyllodes tumor  a diagnosis of fibroadenoma is favored  a focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia is also noted in breast tissue adjacent to the fibroadenoma  and extends to  0 1cm from the margin of resection  dr  melinda lerwill and dr  frederick koerner have reviewed this case and concur with the interpretation  b  breast  left  final margin deep   excision  1  benign breast parenchyma  2  there is no evidence of malignancy  c  breast  left  final margin anterior   excision  1  flat epithelial atypia  2  