accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report  ms 09  removed_accession_id  case  ms 09  removed_accession_id  removed_patient_name  date taken  removed_date source care unit  same day surgery unit path subspecialty service  breast 2 results to  michelle c specht  m d  signed out by  ronald balassanian  m d  clinical data  the patient is a 38 year old woman undergoing left breast needle localization for a breast mass  final diagnosis  a  breast  left   excision 1  cellular fibroadenoma with mild usual ductal hyperplasia  2  fibrocystic change with sclerosing adenosis  see note  note  sections of the left breast excision reveal a fibroepithelial lesion measuring 1 0cm in maximum diameter which does not extend to the margins of excision  there is a pericanalicular growth pattern with duct structures compressed by surrounding stroma  the lesion is mostly well circumscribed with a pushing border  however  there is a focus where the border is ill defined  notably  a leaf like pattern of growth to indicate a phyllodes tumor is not present  the epithelial component is mildly proliferative with some ducts expanded by enlarged polymorphous ductal cells with overlapping nuclei and prominent nucleoli  the stomal component has moderately increased cellularity with enlarged spindle cells tapered ends  irregular nuclear contours  open vesicular chromatin and prominent nucleoli  a few mitotic figures are noted with three mitotic figures counted in ten high powered fields  3 mit 10 hpfs   we considered diagnoses of benign phyllodes tumor and of juvenile fibroadenoma for this lesion  however  the morphology and in particular the absence of a leaf like pattern of growth  rules against a diagnosis of phyllodes tumor  similarly  the small size and clinical presentation rules against a diagnosis of juvenile fibroadenoma  overall  the morphologic findings are compatible with a cellular fibroadenoma with areas of mild usual ductal hyperplasia  gross description  received  labeled remove_patient_name   remove_mrn and  left breast needle loc   is a removed_date x removed_date x 1 0cm portion of tan red fibrofatty tissue with a localization wire in place  a short black stitch designates the superior margin  and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin  the posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green and the inferior yellow  the specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a removed_date x removed_date x 0 8cm indurated gray white mass which comes to 0 1cm of the superior margin  0 1cm of the posterior margin  0 1cm of the anterior margin  0 8cm of the inferior margin  0 8cm of the medial margin  and 1 3cm of the lateral margin  laterally  adjacent to the mass  is a removed_date x removed_date x 0 3cm region of hemorrhage  no other gross abnormalities are identified  and the specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral as  removed_accession_id   with the medial end en face  the lateral en face as  removed_accession_id   and the entire mass as  removed_accession_id   final diagnosis by ronald balassanian m d   electronically signed on sunday removed_month 11   removed_case_id  at 04 42 22pm by his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the final diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  part   breast  left   excision  report_end  , Present.
