 removed_case_id  meisner anne m 28 f  reg ref 01 08    removed_case_id   wic maguire cynthia puyod m d                                                                                             specimen   removed_accession_id   removed_case_id  sout received  01 08 07  removed_case_id  spec type    clinical diagnosis   history  palpable lump  upper outer quadrant right breast removed_date x removed_date x 0 8cm  with calcifications  rule out carcinoma edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj gross description  the specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  guided breast biopsy  right breast  and contains an aqua cassette which is designated on the specimen requisition form to contain the specimen microcalcifications  it contains two firm  tan pink  glistening needle biopsies measuring 1 5cm  in length  0 2cm  in diameter and 2cm  in length  0 2cm  in diameter  resubmitted in cassette 1  2x all  also present within the container are an additional five firm  tan pink  glistening needle biopsies ranging in size from 0 4cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter to 1 6cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter  submitted in cassette 2  5x all  dictated by  lv edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord diagnosis  right breast  upper outer quadrant  needle biopsy  ductal carcinoma in situ  grade removed_date with comedocarcinoma  sarcomatoid focus associated with the ductal carcinoma in situ  edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj descriptive comment  note  pankeratin stain in the sarcomatoid focus is negative in the atypical cells  the slides from this case were referred to dr  frederick koerner of the massachusetts general hospital  who agrees with this diagnosis  his further comments are as follows   i agree with your thoughts about this case  the sections of this core biopsy specimen show a high grade ductal carcinoma in situ and several small irregular clusters of carcinoma cells  which suggest the presence of conventional invasive carcinoma  the diagnostic problem centers on the nature of an adjacent nodule of anaplastic spindle cells  they appear large and they possess large  pleomorphic nuclei  i found many mitotic figures in just a short search  i feel certain that the spindle cells represent a malignant neoplasm  but i cannot offer a more definite diagnosis based on this small sample  i suspect that full evaluation of an excision specimen will reveal that the tumor represents a spindle cell  metaplastic  carcinoma  but less likely possibilities include high grade phyllodes tumor and sarcoma  the lack of keratin staining of the spindle cells in this sample does not argue against the diagnosis of spindle cell carcinoma  for these tumors often show only focal keratin expression  furthermore  antibodies directed against high molecular weight keratin such as keratin 903 seem to offer the greatest sensitivity for detecting the protein in these carcinomas   final diagnosis by  richard j  sampson  m d  edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj notes  removed_date  all 12 slides ret d from mgh  jam  cr  removed_date  report faxed from mgh  jam removed_date  dr  koerner s letter rec d  djd removed_date  12 slides to dr  frederick koerner  mgh for opinion per rjs djd co edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murjcodes   removed_accession_id    right breast  n breanbx    breanbx breanbx  removed_accession_id     breanbx intraductal car breanbx  removed_accession_id     breanbx comedocarcinoma breanbx  removed_accession_id     breanbx with grade edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murjcopies to  semine a  alan m d  dept  of radiology newton  ma  removed_case_id   617 243  removed_case_id  maguire cynthia puyod m d  65 walnut st  ste 590 wellesley  ma  removed_